Hidden Leaf: the films' sound in order, one packet at a time. UN5's PCM callback (0x1046A0, the ezmovie one) copies a whole
packet or nothing and returns 0 when its sound buffer is full; the libmpeg stops the demux on that packet and offers it again.
The runtime dropped it: the packets have odd sizes (4077, 4063 bytes), so each drop put the stream off its 512-byte L/R blocks
by an odd count and it played as full-scale noise until the next odd drop (the boot's "hiss"). Now the sound events wait in a
FIFO, one callback in flight; a refused one is offered again at the next demux call, which takes no new data until then. The
packet's bytes are saved when queued: if the game's ring has new data there by then, the copy goes to 0x7C000 (the top of the
kernel's RAM, unused by the HLE kernel, checked all zero; the callback takes an address past the ring's end as wrapped).
HL_MPEG_AUDIO_DROP=1: the old way.

