+        // Hidden Leaf: the movie sound one packet at a time, in order. The game's PCM callback (UN5 0x1046A0, the ezmovie
+        // one) copies all of a packet or nothing and returns 0 when its sound buffer is full; the libmpeg then stops the
+        // demux on that packet and hands it again later. Dropped here, the packets (odd sizes: 4077, 4063 bytes) put the
+        // stream off its 512-byte L/R blocks by an odd count and it played as full-scale noise until the next drop
+        // (HL_MPEG_AUDIO_DROP=1: the old way). A held packet makes the demux take no new data (backpressure), so the
+        // game's ring keeps its bytes; a 64-byte hash checks it anyway before each retry.
